A section header is recognized only if it is exactly two words and the first word is spelled in
upper case.  The header with an extra word and the header in lower case are instead treated as
directory lines in the "GITROOT:" section:  each is a relative directory name followed by a module.
"~/after" therefore belongs to the "GITROOT:" section.  The goal file records the current (wrong)
behavior; a line that resembles a section header, but is not a valid one, should be reported as an
error rather than silently treated as a directory.

Bug report: https://github.com/plume-lib/multi-version-control/issues/613
